# Copy this file to backend/.env and fill in the values.
#
#   cd backend
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# backend/.env is gitignored — it never gets committed or pushed. Keep the real
# values out of chats, screenshots and commit messages.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DATABASE_URL — shared PostgreSQL, so every machine sees the same data
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave this unset to use the local backend/data.json file instead. That copy is
# per-machine: applications and feedbacks entered on one computer never reach
# the other.
#
# Where to get it: Render dashboard → your database (skillup-academy-db) →
# Connections → "External Database URL". Use the EXTERNAL one. The internal URL
# only resolves inside Render's own network and will simply time out from home.
#
# ⚠️  This is the live database. A local server pointed at it reads and writes
#     the same rows the public site uses — applications sent by real visitors
#     included. Anything you change locally, including through the admin panel,
#     is immediately live.
#
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host.oregon-postgres.render.com/dbname

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Admin panel
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ADMIN_USERNAME defaults to "admin" when unset.
# ADMIN_USERNAME=admin
#
# Production must use ADMIN_PASSWORD_HASH (bcrypt). Generate one with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('bcryptjs').hashSync('your-password', 10))"
# ADMIN_PASSWORD_HASH=
#
# Dev-only plaintext fallback. The server logs a warning when it is used, and it
# must never be set on a deployment that is reachable from the internet.
# ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CORS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The origin allowed to call this API. Unset means any origin, which is fine
# locally and wrong in production.
# ALLOWED_ORIGIN=https://your-site.netlify.app

# Port the API listens on. Defaults to 8000; Render sets this itself.
# PORT=8000
